  "provenance_notes": [
    "Table S1 (paper) lists k-5 = 0.02 s^-1; the deposited SBML uses k_5 = 0.2 s^-1 (10x). SBML value used (executable source of truth); discrepancy flagged.",
    "Table S1 does not list k_4; SBML has k_4 = 0.1 s^-1.",
    "k3 and k8/k9 are one-sided bounds in the paper (0.015-0.016 and < 0.015 per kinetochore, 'in-silico parameter study'); the SBML fixes 0.015 and 0.014 per kinetochore.",
    "Securin(0) = 0.1 uM from the SBML; the paper normalizes securin to 1 at prometaphase onset in Fig. 5A.",
    "CyclinB(0) = 0 in the SBML, so the cyclinB branch (reaction 4) is inert; the paper states securin is the modeled output signal.",
    "Reaction 13 (Mad2 -> empty set at rate kattach) breaks strict Mad2 conservation; this is the paper's published convention for Mad2 sequestration/movement to the spindle.",
    "KinU is a count (92), not a concentration; all kinetic laws multiply by compartment=1 so units are internally consistent."
